.TH qsh-session-open 1  "open 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
qsh\-session\-open \- Create a session on a pinned host. Without a command after `\-\-` the remote login shell is started
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBqsh session open\fR [\fB\-\-env\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-jsonl\fR] [\fB\-\-term\fR] [\fB\-\-cols\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-rows\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIHOST\fR> [\fICOMMAND\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a session on a pinned host. Without a command after `\-\-` the remote login shell is started
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-env\fR \fI<NAME=VALUE>\fR
Extra environment variable for the session (`NAME=VALUE`). Repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit a single `qsh.cli/v1` JSON envelope on stdout instead of human\-readable text
.TP
\fB\-\-jsonl\fR
Emit newline\-delimited JSON on stdout (reserved for streaming commands; non\-streaming commands emit a single line, same as `\-\-json`)
.TP
\fB\-\-term\fR \fI<TERM>\fR
`TERM` to export in the session; defaults to the remote\*(Aqs choice
.TP
\fB\-\-cols\fR \fI<N>\fR
Initial terminal width; defaults to the remote\*(Aqs choice
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase diagnostic verbosity on stderr (`\-v` info, `\-vv` debug, `\-vvv` trace). Never affects stdout (`docs/CLI.md` §2.2)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress diagnostic output on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-rows\fR \fI<N>\fR
Initial terminal height; defaults to the remote\*(Aqs choice
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fIHOST\fR>
Host alias from the trust store (`qsh trust list`)
.TP
[\fICOMMAND\fR]
The program and its arguments, after `\-\-`. Omit for the login shell
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
